# All You Need Is Love, verse (figure 118.2)
# Pollack counts the bars out above the chart (4 3 4 3 / 4 4 4 3); the 3-beat bars are marked <3>.
# The Bassline moves in parallel tenths with the tune, as the essay says. "(V)" under the bass D in
# bars 2 and 4 is a passing V over the e chord; "4/2" under the C in bar 7 makes the held D a V 4/2.
#? Last bar: Pollack types five bass notes (B C D D E) in three beats; equal shares are used, but on
#? the record this is probably the dotted D-E-G rising motif the essay describes. Check the rhythm.
